# A record whose head is an ordinary Structure launches it in code separated from its data (the author 2026-11-11,
# LMX_blog/2026-11-11.md#structure-call-by-name; R21, R22; plan M11 5b): in a callable's code `Own()` runs Own over
# itself, `Bump(Counter)` and `Bump(data := Counter)` run Bump over the data Counter -- the one argument data, given by
# position or by name.
Own: (int: n 5; n := n + 1)
Bump: (n := n + 1)
Counter: (int: n 0)
fn: f () int
    Own()
    Own()
    Bump(Counter)
    Bump(data := Counter)
    return: Own\n * 10 + Counter\n
end: f
int: seen f()
